ENTRY 11263 {"id":11263,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"docs/repo-workspace.md:34:  once), then its secrets (found by stored id and by name), then the claim and PVC. Repeatable after a crash.\ndocs/research/phase1-apis.md:125:  PVC naming: \"named after the template and the Sandbox, joined by a hyphen, owned by the Sandbox ... kept while suspended or retained after expiry; garbage collected when the Sandbox object is deleted\" (`sandbox_types.go:296-311`). Sandbox's list is immutable after creation.\ndocs/research/phase1-apis.md:136:  volumeClaimTemplatesPolicy: Overrides   # or Allowed, so the claim may add a PVC\ndocs/research/phase1-apis.md:168:Not validated against a cluster; only the field names were checked against the CRD/Go types. The template and claim fields come from the cited upstream files; the pieces I merged (service + PVC policy + warm pool replicas 0) are UNVERIFIED as a working combination.\ndocs/network-policy.md:45:| orchestrator, e2e driver, Postgres | kube-apiserver | 443, 6443 | claims, pods, PVCs; suites; CNPG instance manager | C orchestrator/e2e-driver/postgres-egress-kube-apiserver |\ndocs/session-api.md:158:  says to delete the claim and its PVC.\ndocs/session-api.md:168:  died gets its sandbox Pod replaced (the claim and PVC stay), because a `setsid` child escapes the process-group kill.\ndocs/session-api.md:204:sandbox, PVC and OneCLI agent alive, and the orphan sweep never touches a `deleting` session. A failing delete is\ndocs/session-api.md:213:PVCs `workspace-pi-conv-<n>` without a claim, and OneCLI agents `pi-session-<uuid>` with their secrets, when the session\ndocs/decisions/0004-idle-suspend.md:29:  `spec.operatingMode` to `Suspended` removed the Pod within seconds, the PVC (same uid) and the claim stayed, the\ndocs/decisions/0003-recycle-pod-on-interrupt.md:15:When the orchestrator knows a command was interrupted, it **deletes the sandbox Pod, never the claim or the PVC**. The\ndocs/decisions/00